NAME "The composer banner at boot, in a non-default mode"
WINDOW 100 34
TARGET both
SETTINGS '{"agentMode":"plan","showTips":false}'

# Why this scene exists.
#
# Scene 47 captures the composer placeholder "Plan mode: ..." and
# "Accept-edits mode: ..." *after* a shift+tab, on both panes. Scene 50
# captured a boot with no `agentMode` key, and there the two panes differed:
#
#     agy      "> "                                        (no banner)
#     pigasus  "> Auto mode: edits & safe commands ..."    (banner)
#
# That pair is ambiguous. It is consistent with two different rules:
#
#   R1  auto is the default, and the default mode draws no banner, so auto
#       is silent while plan and accept-edits are not — this fires at boot.
#   R2  no banner is drawn at boot for *any* mode; the banner appears only
#       once the user changes the mode mid-session.
#
# Both explain scene 50. They differ exactly here: boot straight into `plan`.
# Under R1 agy draws "Plan mode: ..." at boot; under R2 it draws nothing and
# only pigasus does.
#
# The status row is in the same snapshot because it discriminates the same
# way: `plan` carries a prefix and `auto` does not, so the pair (prefix,
# banner) has to agree on the side agy is on.

BOOT_BOTH
WAIT_READY 15s
SLEEP 1500ms
SNAPSHOT "01_boot_in_plan"

DIFF
CLEANUP
